# Git policy (agents)

**Classic flow:** related tasks share a branch → few meaningful commits → **one PR when the code cluster is ready**. 
Never push directly to `main` (**except TEMP** below). Prefer **squash merge** so `main` stays readable.

**TEMP (Actions billing limit, see `docs/12-development.md` § CI):** auto CI off (`workflow_dispatch` only). After local tests pass, agents **may push related clusters straight to `main`** — no PR. Revert to classic PR flow when Actions minutes return and `ci.yml` triggers are restored.

## Branch

- `phase/N-short-slug`, `epic/P?-E?-short`, or `feat/…` for a **coherent code cluster**.
- Do **not** open a separate PR for every micro-task, handoff, or PM docs pass.

## Commits

- Commit when a **coherent unit** is ready (prefer batching related Task IDs).
- Handoff files are **required on disk** for the role pipeline — they do **not** require their own commit or PR.
- Leave the tree dirty across Dev→QA→PM on the same cluster until the unit (or PR) is ready.
- Still commit before push/PR (no huge unreviewed dump).

## When to open a PR

Open **push + `gh pr create --base main`** only when **all** of these hold:

1. There is **substantive code** (crates / apps) in the branch vs `main`, **and**
2. Either the **code cluster is Done** (QA Pass + enough to ship), **or** the user explicitly says «PR» / «открой PR» / «закрой epic», **and**
3. There is **no open PR** already for this head branch.

**Do not open a PR for:**
- handoffs only (`docs/handoffs/*`)
- roadmap / canvas / status docs only
- a second PR that duplicates an existing open/merged PR on the same branch tip
- stale `SPRINT-GATE` / `PR-GATE` markers that are already MERGED/ARCHIVED

**Docs separately:** PM can update `SPRINT_ROADMAP.md`, `12-development.md`, catalog notes, canvas **without** a dedicated PR — fold into the next code PR, or a small docs commit later when the user asks. Handoffs may land with that same docs/code commit.

## Roles (git only)

| Role | Git expectation |
| :--- | :--- |
| Dev/UX | Handoff on disk. Commit with the code unit — not after every build. |
| QA | Handoff on disk. Usually no commit; fold test fixes into the cluster. |
| PM | Docs/canvas on disk. No PR just to mark Done; ride next code PR or docs batch. |

## Orchestrated multi-role runs

`прогони pipeline` / `сделай сам`: emit handoff files per role. Git: **one (or few) commits** for the finished **code** cluster, then **at most one** PR — not commit-per-role and not PR-per-handoff.

## Hook

`.cursor/hooks/git-policy-stop.sh` may nudge on a **very dirty** tree with **code** changes, or an **active** (non-archived) gate + user intent. It must **not** treat handoff-only dirt or archived gates as «open a PR now».
